A byte appended to the log does not raise its line.
A reader armed on the line, which was low, never hears of the byte;
an Irq armed on the log's line has nothing untaken behind it.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: armed log irq while the log has bytes untaken

diff --git a/kernel/klog.c b/kernel/klog.c
index 722213d..e8ea9a8 100644
--- a/kernel/klog.c
+++ b/kernel/klog.c
@@ -63,8 +63,3 @@ void klog_append(char c)
     header->head++;
-    if (quiet) {
-        struct irq *irq = line_binding(LOG_IRQ_LINE);
-        if (irq != NULL && irq_armed(irq)) {
-            klog_signal(irq);
-        }
-    }
+    (void)quiet;
 }
